    "distinct_from_closed_families": [
      "The closed RSI14 rule compares recent gain and loss magnitudes; MACD compares two exponentially weighted close levels and then smooths their spread.",
      "The closed OBV rule accumulates signed volume and compares simple averages; MACD uses no volume and a second-stage EMA signal.",
      "The closed monthly time-series momentum rule uses one twelve-month endpoint return and monthly decisions; MACD uses daily exponentially decaying path memory and daily state.",
      "The closed Donchian and Supertrend rules require extrema or true range and band state; MACD uses close only and no channel, ATR or stop."
    ],
    "excluded_reinterpretations": [
      "MACD 12/26/9 is the primary policy. Fast lengths 10 and 14 with slow 26 and signal 9 are rejection-only neighbors and cannot replace a failed primary.",
